  "Reported only: test-sequence statistics are never used for any choice (plan Phase 3 step 2).",
  "iei: v2e distributes the events of one pixel within one (interpolated) frame interval in a fixed timestamp 'pyramid' (v2e README); short inter-event intervals of v2e reflect this artefact and the 0.75 ms timestamp cap (D-025), not sensor physics (D-027).",
  "hot_fraction: one sample per 500 ms block, so its histogram rests on n_blocks samples per group (see n_samples.hot_fraction); treat its W1 as coarse.",
  "Both streams use identical windows, blocks and spans; real DVS hot pixels and noise are kept (no filtering of either stream).",
  "v2e inherits the APS frames' dynamic range, blur and frame rate; nothing here measures HDR or latency behaviour."
